# Git workflow

After substantive changes (features, fixes, refactors, docs/rules that ship with code):

1. Create a branch from up-to-date `main`: `feature/…`, `fix/…`, or `chore/…`
2. Commit only relevant files (never `.env`, `*.db`, privacy-export JSON, model artifacts)
3. Push with `-u` and open a PR via `gh pr create`
4. Merge into `main` when checks/review pass (`gh pr merge`), then switch back to `main` and pull

Do not commit directly on `main` for substantive work. Do not force-push `main`. Skip this flow only for trivial one-line typos when the user says so.
